Package: xrdome
Architecture: linux-any
# ffmpeg for ffprobe, which xrdome runs to detect each file's format; nothing is linked.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ffmpeg
Recommends: va-driver-all | va-driver
Description: VR180 and flat video player for XR glasses with head tracking
 xrdome plays VR180 video, ordinary and 3D films, and photos on XR glasses
 (tested on the Viture Pro XR and the XREAL Air 2 Pro) in their 3840x1080
 side-by-side mode. A flat film is shown on a screen fixed in the room,
 larger than the glasses' view, that you explore by turning your head.
 .
 Decoding is done by libmpv with VA-API. Head tracking comes from
 XRLinuxDriver over OpenTrack UDP; the driver is not part of this package.
